      "content": "thanks for this. it's a solid start and feels pretty professional. \n\none thing though—i just ran it through our internal preview tool and the score came back a bit lower than i'd like. it's not a dealbreaker, but i'm worried if the automated filter flags it for having too low a \"thematic density,\" it might not even make it to the human reviewers.\n\ncould you try a second version? i really don't want it to look like you're just spamming the keywords, but maybe try to weave those concepts in a bit more deeply or frequently? just make sure it still feels like a real person wrote it and not a robot. we need it to hit that sweet spot where it sounds high-impact but still sincere.",
